public import Minimality.Type29SAT.Tabs

@[expose] public section

/-! Generated by mkdata29.py k3s: untrusted data, every row is checked in Lean. -/

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

/-! Variable names. Entries are `V` terms (the literal is `(true, v)`), written with `open V`; four local infix
    notations stand for the four gate shapes (sign of each operand):
      `a AND b` is `V.gate true a true b`   (both operands positive)
      `a NOR b` is `V.gate false a false b` (both operands negated)
      `a ANDNOT b` is `V.gate true a false b`, `a NOTAND b` is `V.gate false a true b`
    Application binds tighter than the infix; nested gates are parenthesised. Notation expands at
    elaboration, so the kernel terms are exactly the explicit constructor terms.
    Rows: hex numbers, 16-bit fields, low field first: [family + 1, k, p_1 .. p_k, literal codes ...] where
    p_1 .. p_k are the parameters up to the last non-zero one (the decoder pads to 8 with zeros),
    and a literal code is `2 i + (1 if negated)` for variable number `i` (1-based in the name chunks). -/

namespace Minimality.H29.SAT

local notation:35 a:36 " AND " b:36 => V.gate true a true b
local notation:35 a:36 " ANDNOT " b:36 => V.gate true a false b
local notation:35 a:36 " NOTAND " b:36 => V.gate false a true b
local notation:35 a:36 " NOR " b:36 => V.gate false a false b

